### Got any other Mapbox-specific code (e.g., `setFog`, `mapboxgl.accessToken`, or plugins you’re unsure about)?  
Drop it here and I’ll tell you the exact MapLibre replacement or workaround.

Below are the most common ways to add a **search-box (geocoder) control** to a map that is built with **Mapbox GL JS v2**.  
I’ve grouped them by the service they talk to, the npm package you’ll use, and a quick “how-to” snippet so you can copy-paste it into your project.

---

## 1️⃣ Use Mapbox’s own Geocoding API (the default choice)

| What you get | How to add it | When to use it |
|--------------|---------------|----------------|
| Full-featured forward-geocoding, autocomplete, biasing, language & country filters. | Install the official plugin **`@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder`** and the CSS that ships with it. | You already have a Mapbox access token and are okay with Mapbox’s rate limits / pricing. |

### Installation

```bash
npm install @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder
# or with yarn: yarn add @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder
```

### Basic usage (ES-modules)

```js
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';               // v2.x
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

// Set your token (required for the API)
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

// Create the geocoder control
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // tells the plugin which map library to use
  placeholder: 'Search places',
  // optional: limit results to a country or language
  // countries: 'us,ca',
  // language: 'en',
  // proximity: { longitude: -122.42, latitude: 37.78 } // bias toward current view
});

// Add it to the map (top-left by default)
map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');

// Optional: react to a result
geocoder.on('result', (e) => {
  console.log('Selected place:', e.result);
});
```

### Customising the UI

* **Position** – `map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-right')`, `'bottom-left'`, etc.  
* **Styling** – Override the CSS classes (`.mapboxgl-ctrl-geocoder`, `.suggestion`) in your own stylesheet.  
* **Bounding-box bias** – Pass `bbox: [west, south, east, north]` in the options to restrict results.  
* **Result handling** – The `result` event gives you the full GeoJSON feature; you can add a marker, fly the camera, etc.

---

## 2️⃣ Use an **open / self-hosted** geocoder and the MapLibre-compatible wrapper

If you want to avoid Mapbox’s usage limits, keep everything open-source, or already run a Nominatim / Photon / Pelias instance, you can pair those services with **`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`** (the same UI component, but it works with any HTTP-compatible geocoder).

| Service | URL pattern (example) | Notes |
|--------|-----------------------|-------|
| **Nominatim** (OSM) | `https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=geojson&q={query}` | Free public instance is for low-volume testing only. Self-host for production. |
| **Photon** (Komoot) | `https://photon.komoot.io/api/?q={query}` | Fast, lightweight, also free for low volume. |
| **Pelias** | `https://pelias.example.com/v1/search?text={query}` | Requires you to run the Pelias stack (or use a hosted provider). |
| **MapTiler Geocoding** | `https://api.maptiler.com/geocoding/{query}.json?key=YOUR_KEY` | Commercial SaaS with generous free tier; works with the same UI. |
| **OpenCage** | `https://api.opencagedata.com/geocode/v1/json?q={query}&key=YOUR_KEY` | Paid service, good global coverage. |

### Installation

```bash
npm install @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder
# plus the CSS (same as the Mapbox plugin)
npm install @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder   # pulls the CSS for you
```

### Example: Nominatim + MapLibre-compatible wrapper

```js
import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';
import MapLibreGeocoder from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

// No token needed for the map itself (you’ll use a non-Mapbox style later)
const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // any non-Mapbox style
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

// Build a simple forward-geocoder that talks to Nominatim
function nominatimGeocoder(query) {
  const url = new URL('https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search');
  url.searchParams.set('format', 'geojson');
  url.searchParams.set('addressdetails', '1');
  url.searchParams.set('q', query);
  // optional: limit, viewbox, bounded, etc.
  return fetch(url)
    .then(res => res.json())
    .then(data => ({
      // The wrapper expects an array of GeoJSON Feature objects
      features: data.features
    }));
}

// Create the control
const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  placeholder: 'Search OSM',
  // The wrapper calls this function for each query
  forwardGeocoder: nominatimGeocoder,
  // Optional: you can also provide a reverseGeocoder if you need it
  // reverseGeocoder: ...
});

map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');

geocoder.on('result', (e) => {
  console.log('Nominatim result:', e.result);
  // Example: fly to the result
  map.flyTo({ center: e.result.geometry.coordinates, zoom: 14 });
});
```

**Why use the wrapper?**  
* The UI (autocomplete dropdown, keyboard navigation, mobile-friendly layout) is exactly the same as the Mapbox plugin, so you don’t have to redesign your UI.  
* It works with any service that returns **GeoJSON FeatureCollection** (or you can adapt the response in `forwardGeocoder`).  

---

## 3️⃣ Build a **custom UI** (no external plugin)

If you prefer a lightweight, fully custom search box (e.g., you already have a UI framework like React, Vue, or Svelte), you can call any geocoding endpoint yourself and then move the map.

### Minimal vanilla-JS example (Nominatim)

```html
<input id="search" type="text" placeholder="Search…" />
<div id="suggestions"></div>
<div id="map" style="width:100%;height:400px;"></div>

<script type="module">
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

const input = document.getElementById('search');
const suggestions = document.getElementById('suggestions');

let abortCtrl = null;

input.addEventListener('input', async (e) => {
  const q = e.target.value.trim();
  if (!q) { suggestions.innerHTML = ''; return; }

  // Cancel previous request
  if (abortCtrl) abortCtrl.abort();
  abortCtrl = new AbortController();

  const url = new URL('https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search');
  url.searchParams.set('format', 'json');
  url.searchParams.set('addressdetails', '1');
  url.searchParams.set('limit', '5');
  url.searchParams.set('q', q);

  try {
    const resp = await fetch(url, { signal: abortCtrl.signal });
    const results = await resp.json();

    suggestions.innerHTML = results.map(r => `
      <div class="item" data-lon="${r.lon}" data-lat="${r.lat}">
        ${r.display_name}
      </div>
    `).join('');
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.name !== 'AbortError') console.error(err);
  }
});

suggestions.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  const item = e.target.closest('.item');
  if (!item) return;
  const lon = parseFloat(item.dataset.lon);
  const lat = parseFloat(item.dataset.lat);
  map.flyTo({ center: [lon, lat], zoom: 14 });
  suggestions.innerHTML = '';
});
</script>
```

*Pros*: No extra CSS, no extra bundle size.  
*Cons*: You lose the polished autocomplete UI, keyboard navigation, and built-in result-format handling that the official plugins provide.

---

## 4️⃣ Summary – Which option should you pick?

| Situation | Recommended approach |
|-----------|----------------------|
| **Already paying for Mapbox & have a token** | Use **`@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder`** – simplest, full-featured, works out-of-the-box. |
| **Want to stay open-source / avoid Mapbox fees** | Use **`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`** + an open geocoder (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, MapTiler Geocoding, etc.). |
| **Running your own geocoder service** | Same wrapper (`@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`) with a custom `forwardGeocoder` function that points at your API. |
| **Need a tiny, framework-specific UI** | Build a **custom search component** and call the geocoder API directly (React, Vue, Svelte, etc.). |
| **You plan to migrate away from Mapbox GL JS v2 later** | Start with the **MapLibre-compatible wrapper** now; it works with both Mapbox GL JS v2 (it only needs `mapboxgl` for the UI) and with MapLibre GL JS after migration. |

---

## 5️⃣ Quick checklist for a smooth integration

1. **Install the right package** (`@mapbox/...` for Mapbox, `@maplibre/...` for open services).  
2. **Add the CSS** (`import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';`).  
3. **Provide an access token** *only* if you’re using Mapbox’s own Geocoding API.  
4. **Configure the geocoder** (placeholder, language, country, proximity, bbox) to match your UX.  
